  "final_message": "Status: reproduced, then fixed. Slot `<template>`s whose names start with an underscore are used again when the child component is patched without the optimized path. The new tests pass, and the full unit suite passes apart from one unrelated timing test (see Verification).\n\n## Reproduction\n\nI decoded the playground link from the report. `App` renders `<BaseLayout>` containing a `v-if` slot template (`#randomslotname`) and a `<SubComponent>`. `SubComponent` has `<template #title>` and `<template #_duration>`. I rebuilt that structure as a test in `packages/vue/__tests__/index.spec.ts`.\n\nCommand:\n\n    npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/index.spec.ts -t \"underscore\"\n\nBefore the fix, it exits 1:\n\n    expected '<div><p>random</p><b>title</b><i>defa\u2026' to be '<div><p>random</p><b>title</b><b>dura\u2026'\n\nThe `title` slot is replaced, but `_duration` shows its default content, which is exactly the report. The same test passes when `_duration` is renamed to `duration`, so the leading underscore is the trigger.\n\n## Cause\n\nCommit 5d166f3 (in 3.5.14) changed the check in `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts`:\n\n    - if (optimized || key !== '_')\n    + if (optimized || !isInternalKey(key))\n\n`isInternalKey` is true for any key starting with `_`. The `v-if` slot template makes `BaseLayout`'s slots dynamic. Its `<slot>` outlet then renders `SubComponent` in the non-optimized (BAIL) mode. In that mode `assignSlots` dropped every `_`-prefixed slot, including real ones like `_duration`.\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` I added `isSlotsMarker`, which matches only the compiler markers `_` and `__`.\n\n- **`assignSlots`:** it now uses `isSlotsMarker`. This covers mount, update and HMR, since all three go through it.\n- **Stale-slot deletion in `updateSlots`:** it also used `isInternalKey`, so a `_`-prefixed slot was never removed once its `v-if` turned false. Before the fix, `<Child><template v-if=\"show\" #_foo>` kept showing its content after `show` became false instead of the fallback. This was already wrong in 3.5.13, but it comes from the same cause, so I fixed it too.\n\nI left `normalizeObjectSlots` on `isInternalKey`. Hand-written object slots with `_` names are skipped there, and an existing test asserts that.\n\n## Tests added\n\n- `packages/vue/__tests__/index.spec.ts`: the report's scenario, including toggling the `v-if`, and a conditional `#_foo` slot that must fall back to its default content when hidden.\n- `packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts`: two tests, one for mount with `_foo` slots in non-optimized mode and one for dynamic `_one`/`_two` slots updated in non-optimized mode.\n\n## Verification\n\n- All new tests fail before the fix.\n- With only the `assignSlots` change, the two update-path tests still fail, so the deletion change is needed.\n- After the fix, `componentSlots.spec.ts` and `index.spec.ts` pass (37 tests).\n- The full `vitest --project unit` run had one failure: `reactivity/computed.spec.ts` \"should not lead to exponential perf cost\" (105ms against a 30ms limit). That is a timing test under load. The file passes when run alone.\n- Prettier and ESLint are clean on the changed files.\n",
